concepts.body:
A Gradle build has two script files at its root:

- `settings.gradle.kts` names the build (`rootProject.name`) and lists subprojects with `include("app", "lib")`. It also configures where plugins come from (`pluginManagement`) and, in modern builds, where dependencies come from (`dependencyResolutionManagement`).
- `build.gradle.kts` configures a project: which **plugins** to apply, which **repositories** to search, and which **dependencies** the code needs.

Scripts use the **Kotlin DSL** (`.kts`, the default since Gradle 8) or the older Groovy DSL (`build.gradle`). The Kotlin DSL is type-safe with IDE completion; the concepts are identical.

A minimal JVM app:

```kotlin
plugins { id("java"); id("application") }
repositories { mavenCentral() }
dependencies { implementation("com.google.guava:guava:33.4.0-jre") }
application { mainClass = "com.acme.App" }
```

Plugins add tasks and conventions. The `java` plugin expects sources in `src/main/java`, tests in `src/test/java` and resources in `src/main/resources`, and defines `compileJava`, `test`, `jar` and `build`. Outputs go to `build/`.

`group` and `version` identify your artifacts. The `java { toolchain { languageVersion = JavaLanguageVersion.of(21) } }` block makes Gradle compile with a specific JDK regardless of which one runs Gradle, which keeps builds reproducible across machines.

concepts.code:
// settings.gradle.kts
rootProject.name = "demo"

// build.gradle.kts
plugins {
    java                                   // or id("java")
    application
}

group = "com.acme"
version = "1.0.0"

repositories { mavenCentral() }

dependencies {
    implementation("com.google.guava:guava:33.4.0-jre")
    testImplementation("org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter:5.11.4")
    testRuntimeOnly("org.junit.platform:junit-platform-launcher")
}

java { toolchain { languageVersion = JavaLanguageVersion.of(21) } }

application { mainClass = "com.acme.App" }

tasks.test { useJUnitPlatform() }

// Layout: src/main/java, src/main/resources, src/test/java; outputs in build/

plugins { `java-library` }

repositories { mavenCentral() }

dependencies {
    api("com.fasterxml.jackson.core:jackson-databind:2.18.3")   // leaks into consumers' compile classpath
    implementation("org.slf4j:slf4j-api:2.0.17")              // internal
    compileOnly("org.projectlombok:lombok:1.18.36")
    annotationProcessor("org.projectlombok:lombok:1.18.36")
    runtimeOnly("ch.qos.logback:logback-classic:1.5.18")      // logging backend, not compiled against
    implementation(project(":core"))                          // another subproject

    constraints {
        implementation("com.google.guava:guava:33.4.0-jre") { because("CVE fix") }
    }
    testImplementation("org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter:5.11.4")
}

// $ ./gradlew dependencies --configuration compileClasspath
// $ ./gradlew dependencyInsight --dependency slf4j-api

plugins { java }
repositories { mavenCentral() }

dependencies {
    testImplementation(platform("org.junit:junit-bom:5.11.4"))
    testImplementation("org.junit.jupiter:junit-jupiter")
    testRuntimeOnly("org.junit.platform:junit-platform-launcher")
}

tasks.test {
    useJUnitPlatform { excludeTags("slow") }
    maxParallelForks = (Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors() / 2).coerceAtLeast(1)
    systemProperty("app.env", "test")
    testLogging {
        events("passed", "skipped", "failed")
        showStandardStreams = true
    }
}

// $ ./gradlew test --tests "com.acme.UserServiceTest" --fail-fast
// $ ./gradlew test --rerun
// report: build/reports/tests/test/index.html

// build.gradle.kts
plugins { java }

println("configuration phase: runs on every build")   // avoid heavy work here

val stage = tasks.register<Copy>("stage") {
    group = "distribution"
    description = "Copies the jar and docs into build/staging"
    from(tasks.named("jar"))                 // implies dependsOn(jar)
    from("docs") { include("*.md") }
    into(layout.buildDirectory.dir("staging"))
}

tasks.register("hello") {
    group = "demo"
    doFirst { println("about to greet") }
    doLast { println("Hello from ${project.name}") }
}

tasks.register<Exec>("gitSha") {
    commandLine("git", "rev-parse", "--short", "HEAD")
}

tasks.named("build") { finalizedBy(stage) }  // stage runs after build
// $ ./gradlew hello     -> configuration phase: ... / about to greet / Hello from demo

// settings.gradle.kts
pluginManagement {
    repositories { gradlePluginPortal(); google(); mavenCentral() }
}
rootProject.name = "shop"

// build.gradle.kts
